<Article title="Methodology" description="How Ohmetry calculators are built and tested." h1="Methodology">
<p>Every calculator is a standalone function with automated tests. Test cases come from worked examples in published standards or from hand calculation, and the expected value is written next to each test.</p><p>Code tables are stored as data with the section number cited. We link to the section and explain it in our own words; we do not reproduce code text.</p><p>Found an error? See <a href='/contact/'>Contact</a>. Every correction is recorded in the <a href='/corrections/'>corrections log</a>.</p><h2>Review and update dates</h2><p>Each calculator and guide shows when its page last changed. A "Reviewed" line appears only after a qualified person has checked that page, and it names them. Pages without it have not had an independent review.</p>
</Article>
